-- title:
--   Volume of a cube of side $h$
-- statement:
--   For a real number $h > 0$ and a point $u \in \mathbb{R}^d$, let $\texttt{cube } h\ u$ denote the
--   cube of side $h$ attached to $u$. Its Lebesgue measure is
--
--   $$\lambda_d\big(\texttt{cube } h\ u\big) \;=\; h^{d},$$
--
--   as an element of $[0,\infty]$.
--
--   Together with the corresponding computations for the closed and half-closed variants, this is the
--   volume normalisation used throughout: the three cube variants attached to the same data differ only
--   by their boundaries and therefore all have measure $h^d$, so any of them may be used as the tile of
--   the lattice tiling without changing a constant.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Strict positivity $h > 0$ is required here, whereas the closed and
--   half-closed variants of the same statement hold under the weaker hypothesis $h \ge 0$; the
--   difference is confined to the degenerate mesh $h = 0$.
-- source:
